WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.325
A test for any vector operation.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.331
Rotate then apply, or apply then rotate: same answer.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.875
ReLU zeroes negatives. Rotated v has none.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.330
Apply first: one, zero. Then rotate: zero, one.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.200
The answers differ by one.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.988
Now try every rotation angle.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.527
Solid is clipped at the axes; the dashed one circles.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.480
So the gap depends on the axes.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.789
The fix: a norm activation.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.071
Tanh squashes only the length.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.317
Direction is kept, and rotation never changes length. Both routes agree.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.229
Green means the check passes.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.122
Scalars ignore rotation, so any function works.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.664
Vectors: mix linearly, multiply by a scalar, rescale by length.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.658
The message: scalar y sub u times vector v sub u, summed.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.462
f of R v equals R times f of v.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.244
Act on lengths and scalars, never on components.
